# Cargo.lock is deliberately TRACKED. This workspace produces a deployed binary,
# and the module stamps its source commit into its health metrics so a running
# process can be traced back to what built it. That identity is only complete if
# the commit also fixes the dependency versions -- otherwise two builds of the
# same commit can link different crates, and "same commit, different behaviour"
# becomes unanswerable at exactly the moment someone is asking. Tracking it also
# means CI tests the dependency set that ships, rather than resolving a fresh one
# nobody has built against.

